      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This is the Shir haKavod (“Hymn of Glory,” also known by its incipit “An’im Zemirot”) attributed to Rabbi Yehudah he-Ḥasid of Regensburg, included at the conclusion of the Shir haYiḥud (first attested in print in Thiengen 1560). This translation by Israel Zangwill, was first published in Arthur Davis and Herbert Adler’s <tei:hi rend="italic">Maḥzor Avodat Ohel Moed: Avodat Yom haKippurim (Evening Service)</tei:hi> (1904), pp. 73-74.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_65702_notes"/>
